    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 9th with a tactical focus on speed and favorable handedness, headlined by **Trea Turner** (75.42) and **Kyle Schwarber** (71.37), our two strongest plays against Freeland. **Trea Turner** benefits from the prime leadoff spot and a positive BvP history, while **Kyle Schwarber** leverages his power profile against a pitcher with a 4.24 xERA in a hitter-friendly environment. We are also leaning heavily into the speed of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.15); despite batting 8th, his matchup against Leiter features a favorable delivery profile for stolen base attempts, keeping him as a high-efficiency play despite the lower lineup placement.\n\nOur mid-tier starters offer steady production, with **Colt Keith** (66.01) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.93) both enjoying platoon advantages against right-handed starters. **Kazuma Okamoto** is particularly well-positioned against Kochanowicz, as the 5.14 xERA suggests a high ceiling for run production in the heart of our order. Meanwhile, **Hyeseong Kim** (61.87) remains a core play despite facing a high-velocity arm in Strider; his efficiency score holds up due to consistent contact trends. We are navigating a thin bench today, as **Junior Caminero** and **Caleb Durbin** are unavailable due to postponements, leaving us without the late-inning pinch-hit upside we typically rely on to mitigate risk.\n\nThe decision to bench our remaining depth, including **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena**, was straightforward given the lack of platoon variance and the rainout constraints. **Yordan Alvarez** (61.66) remains a mandatory start despite a tough draw against Burns; his elite .425 xwOBA provides enough raw talent to overcome a stiff pitching matchup. Aside from the weather-related zeroes from **Junior Caminero** and **Caleb Durbin**, the only remaining concern is **Dillon Dingler** (46.19), whose score is suppressed by Wacha\u2019s efficiency at controlling the running game; however, we are committed to the start to maintain our structural integrity in the catching slot.",
